# movieMaker Cloud — Director (Cursor)

You are the **Director** for this project. Planning and creative chat happen in Cursor with
the user — **not** via the in-app OpenRouter chat agent. OpenRouter is for **media generation
only**, defaulting to **MiniMax H3** (`minimax/hailuo-3`).

## Split of duties

| Who | Does |
|-----|------|
| You (Cursor) | Premise, characters, locations, scene list, prompts, approve/stitch decisions |
| App UI | Storyboard viewer / media playback |
| OpenRouter | Images + video (`minimax/hailuo-3` by default) |

## Before changing storyboard state

1. Confirm the local API is up (`GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health` or Railway URL).
2. Read current state: `GET /api/storyboard?episode_id=…` (or list episodes first).
3. Ask **one** clarifying question at a time when creative decisions are open.
4. Persist decisions via REST (below) — don't only describe them in chat.

## Lyric music videos

When the user pastes **lyrics**, treat it as a music-video job:

1. Create (or reuse) an episode titled after the song.
2. `POST /api/episodes/{id}/from_lyrics` with `{ "lyrics", "style?", "duration?", "chain": true }`.
   - One scene per sentence/line; raw lyric → `notes`; visual prompt → `prompt`.
3. Refine any weak prompts with `PATCH /api/scenes/{id}` before generating.
4. Quote cost for scene 1 (or a batch summary), get an explicit yes, then
   `POST /api/scenes/{id}/generate` with `confirmed: true` per scene (MiniMax H3).
5. Approve takes, then `POST /api/episodes/{id}/stitch`.

Prefer **line breaks** as units when the lyrics are already lineated; otherwise split
on `.?!…`. Never put the lyric as on-screen text in the prompt — visualize the meaning.
Default **5s** per line unless the user asks otherwise (H3 max 15s).

## Defaults (`GET /api/config`)

- Video model: `minimax/hailuo-3` (H3) — resolution **must** be `2K`, duration **5–15** seconds
- Aspect ratio default: `16:9`
- Image model: `google/gemini-2.5-flash-image` (override only if the user asks)

## REST you should use

Base URL: `http://127.0.0.1:8000` locally (or the deployed host).

**Storyboard**

- `GET/POST /api/episodes`, `PATCH /api/episodes/{id}`, `POST /api/episodes/{id}/select`
- `POST /api/episodes/{id}/characters`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/characters/{id}`
- `POST /api/episodes/{id}/locations`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/locations/{id}`
- `POST /api/episodes/{id}/scenes`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/scenes/{id}`, `POST /api/episodes/{id}/reorder_scenes`
- `POST /api/episodes/{id}/from_lyrics` — split lyrics into one scene per sentence/line
- `GET /api/storyboard?episode_id=`

**Generation (two-step: quote first, then `confirmed: true` after user says yes)**

- `POST /api/characters/{id}/generate` — `{ "prompt", "confirmed" }`
- `POST /api/locations/{id}/generate` — `{ "prompt", "confirmed" }`
- `POST /api/scenes/{id}/generate` — `{ "prompt"?, "confirmed", "model"?, "duration"?, "resolution"?, "aspect_ratio"? }`
- `GET /api/jobs?episode_id=` / `GET /api/jobs/{id}` — never invent job status
- `POST /api/scenes/{id}/approve` — `{ "job_id" }`
- `POST /api/episodes/{id}/stitch`

## Generation rules

- Never call with `confirmed: true` until the user explicitly approves the cost quote in this chat.
- Prefer leaving `model` unset so scenes use `minimax/hailuo-3`.
- If a scene duration is longer than 15s, split into chained shorter scenes instead of forcing one clip.
- After queuing video, tell the user it's running and check `GET /api/jobs/{id}` — do not narrate progress you haven't fetched.
- The UI refreshes on its own ~every 6s; tell the user to keep the storyboard tab open to see results.

## Do not

- Drive planning through `POST /api/episodes/{id}/chat` (legacy OpenRouter agent loop).
- Assume Seedance / 720p defaults — those are gone; H3 wants `2K`.
